      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b5f5b1f3-b92c-566f-a1ce-33712b84a8d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hjertestop\n- Places: Copenhagen, Nørrebro, Bispebjerg, Jagtvej 69, Dortheavej 61\n- Organizations: Ungdomshuset, Folkets Hus\n- Topics: underground music scene, autonomist groups, leftist groups\n\nFacts:\n- Ungdomshuset was the popular name of the building formally named Folkets Hus at Jagtvej 69 in Nørrebro, Copenhagen.\n- From 1982 until 2007, Ungdomshuset functioned as an underground music venue and a meeting place for various autonomist and leftist groups.\n- After a prolonged conflict, the Ungdomshuset building at Jagtvej 69 was torn down in 2007.\n- The name Ungdomshuset was later also used for its successor at Dortheavej 61 in the adjacent Bispebjerg neighbourhood.\n- Hjertestop was formed in Copenhagen in the scene around Ungdomshuset.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cbce7185-748a-5e96-b5f4-d71899e450f5",
        "text": "Page: Hjertestop. Sentence: It was formed in Copenhagen, in the scene around Ungdomshuset.\nPage: Ungdomshuset. Sentence: Ungdomshuset (literally \"the Youth House\") was the popular name of the building formally named Folkets Hus (\"House of the People\") located on Jagtvej 69 in Nørrebro, Copenhagen, which functioned as an underground scene venue for music and rendezvous point for varying autonomist and leftist groups from 1982 until 2007 when—after prolonged conflict—it was torn down, and later also for its successor, located on Dortheavej 61 in the adjacent Bispebjerg neighbourhood.",
